import tests/cadkernel/brep_place/emit.dl
function placement input vector at {integer:index}:
    execute:
        return a cad vector3 with x (placement argument index), y (placement argument (index + 1)) and z (placement argument (index + 2))
set place to a cad placement with axes (placement input vector at 7), (placement input vector at 10) and (placement input vector at 13) at (placement input vector at 16)
set scale to the cad scale of place
emit placement flag (scale's valid)
if scale's valid:
    emit placement number (scale's value)
emit placement flag (place reflects cad orientation)
emit placement point (the cad image of (place test point [0.2,-0.3,0.7]) under place)
emit placement point (the cad direction of (place test point [0.2,-0.3,0.7]) under place)
emit placement flag (place = (the cad clone of place))
emit placement flag (place = (the cad identity placement))
set original to place test body ((placement argument 0) as an integer) with pcurves ((placement argument 2) as an integer) from (placement argument 4) to (placement argument 5)
damage place test original with ((placement argument 1) as an integer) and (placement argument 6)
emit placement body original
emit placement samples of original within (placement argument 3)
set moved to the cad transformed original by place
emit placement flag (moved's valid)
if moved's valid:
    emit placement body (moved's value)
    emit placement samples of (moved's value) within (placement argument 3)
